# DIAGNOSTICS

A rules file is parsed up to its first error, the rulesets before it kept.
The errors are 9front's words, after the file and line of each file of the include stack: `unknown object kind`, `unknown verb is`, `malformed rule`, `VERB not valid verb for object OBJECT`, `too many ports`, `illegal port name send`, `ruleset has more than one client or start action`, `ruleset must have patterns and actions`, `malformed include statement`, `can't open FILE for inclusion`, `include stack too deep; max 10`, and `regexp RE: ` with why the expression is wrong.

# BUGS

`^` holds only at the start of the data and after a newline, also when a click's match is tried from further in, where 9front's holds at the place it is tried from.
A port declared in quotes with a blank in it is listed without them, as 9front does, so the listing does not read back the same.
